th and Shri Hrinkar Parshwanath फोटो 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" class=\"object-cover\" style=\"position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent\" sizes=\"(min-width: 640px) 33vw, 50vw\" srcSet=\"/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=256&amp;q=75 256w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_7725.jpeg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></div></div><article class=\"prose-none space-y-4 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.85] text-ink\"><p>18. Shri Muleva Parshwanath</p><p>Main Deity: An image of Bhagwan Muleva Parshwanath in the padmasana posture, white in color, approximately 28.5 inches tall and 22 inches wide, stands beside the image of the main deity, Shri Adinath Bhagwan. This is in Ahmedabad.</p><p>Location: This is on Relief Road in Ahmedabad city.</p><p>History: This image of Muleva Parshwanath is believed to be 200-300 years old. About 200-300 years ago, a family of Shethjis of the Shrimali Visha caste built a temple in Idalpur (a suburb of Ahmedabad) and formally installed the image of Muleva Parshwanath there. It is believed that over time the temple must have fallen into disrepair, and this image of Muleva Parshwanath was brought to Panjrapole and installed in the temple of Bhagwan Adinath. Today&#x27;s Haripura was earlier known as Idalpur. The image of Muleva Parshwanath is very powerful, striking and beautiful. Devotees who worship this image regularly experience its influence. Many devotees in Ahmedabad begin their daily routine after worshipping at this temple of Muleva Parshwanath. It is believed that no devotee can continuously worship this image of Muleva Parshwanath for 6 months. This temple is managed by the Seth Hathisingh Kesarisingh Trust. The temple was recently rebuilt without moving the images. This impressive temple is well worth a visit. This temple is also known as the &quot;Moraiya Parshwanath Temple.&quot;</p><p>Other Temples: Ahmedabad has more than 400 temples.</p><p>Directions: Ahmedabad is a very famous city of Gujarat. It is well connected by rail, road and air to all cities of India.</p><p>Scripture References: Muleva Parshwanath is mentioned in &quot;365 Shri Parshwadev Jin Nammala,&quot; &quot;Shri Sankeshwar Parshwanath Chhand,&quot; &quot;108 Naam Garbhit Shri Parshwanath Bhavan,&quot; and others. There is an image of Muleva (Moraiya) Parshwanath at the Jiravala crossroads.</p><p>Hymn of Praise: Who is the root of all prosperity and success, and the root of all progress, who is the root of the wealth, peace and happiness of Rajnagari (Ahmedabad), whose powerful darshan draws devotees here every day -- &quot;I bow with devotion to Shri Muleva Prabhu Parshwa.&quot;</p><p>Chanting Mantra: Om Hrim Arh Shri Muleva Parshwanathaya Namah.</p><p>Trust: Shri Muleva Parshwanath Shwetambar Jain Tirth, Relief Road, near Panjrapole, Ahmedabad - 380001, State of Gujarat, India. Phone: 079-22123704.</p><p>Some further verses are also recorded following the Shri 108 Parshwanath Stuti, which mention the names of Lords Parshwanath such as Sukhsagara, Muhari, Posina, Shankheshwara, Vighnapahari, Nagphana, Kalyan Paras, Manoranjan and Sultan, offering salutations to Shankheshwar Parshwanath.</p><p>19. Shri Hrinkar Parshwanath</p><p>This temple is located in Kalushi ni Pol, Kalupur, Ahmedabad-380001.</p><p>Main Deity: The main deity of this temple is Bhagwan Sambhavnath. In the padmasana posture, a beautiful black-colored image, 25 centimeters tall, set within a beautifully carved parikar, is that of Bhagwan Hrinkar Parshwanath. Behind the image is a canopy of 7 serpent hoods. This image is in the basement, beside the image of Bhagwan Chintamani Parshwanath.</p><p>Location: This is in the temple of Bhagwan Sambhavnath in Kalushi ni Pol, Ahmedabad.</p><p>History: In mantra literature, &quot;Hrim&quot; is considered a mantra-seed (bija). This mantra-seed contains within it the establishment of the twenty-four Jineshwars. Mantra scripture describes a method of meditating on Lord Parshwanath positioned at the center of the syllable &quot;Hrim,&quot; for the practice of numerous yantras and the contemplation of mantras. As though the Lord had manifested in a radiant form directly from such meditation, this image resides in the basement (bhoyaru) of the shrine of Shri Sambhavnath Bhagwan in Kalushi ni Pol, beside Shri Chintamani Parshwanath Prabhu. This Lord, established in the form of &quot;Hrim,&quot; is renowned by the name Hrinkar Parshwanath. Since ancient times, Jainism has existed in Gujarat with a large population of Jains living here. The holiest Jain temples -- such as Shatrunjay Mahatirth, Girnar Tirth, and Shankheshwar Tirth -- are in Gujarat. Most Jain pilgrimage sites are in Gujarat. The image of the main deity, Shri Sambhavnath Bhagwan, bears an inscription of Vikram Samvat 1527, and the image of the main deity of the upper floor, Shri Shantinath, bears an inscription of Vikram Samvat 1670. This indicates that this temple is more than 500 years old. The old temple was renovated in Vikram Samvat 2020, and the images were reconsecrated on the 10th day of the month of Shravan in Vikram Samvat 2021, by the revered hands of Acharya Shri Jambusurishwarji.</p><p>1. The main temple of Hrinkar Parshwanath is in Kalushi Pol, Ahmedabad. 2. In the city of Dungarpur, there is a metal image of Shri Hrinkar Parshwanath in the home temple of Shri Gordhandasji Patwa, which was installed by the revered hands of Acharya Shri Vijaysurishwarji in the latter half of the 17th century. 3. In Belgaum, Karnataka, there is a chariot-shaped temple of Bhagwan Shri Hrinkar Parshwanath. This temple was built by the Shri Rajasthan Jain Shwetambar Murtipujak Trust, and the image was installed in the month of Paush Vadi in Vikram Samvat 2057...</p></article><nav class=\"mt-14 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-sandstone-deep/60 pt-6\"><a class=\"group flex items-center gap-1.5 font-ui text-sm text-ink-soft hover:text-maroon transition-colors\" href=\"/en/tirtha/tirtha-020\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-left h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m15 18-6-6 6-6\"></path></svg><span class=\"max-w-[10rem] truncate sm:max-w-xs\">Shri Shamla Parshwanath</span></a><a class=\"group flex items-center gap-1.5 text-right font-ui text-sm text-ink-soft hover:text-maroon transition-colors\" href=\"/en/tirtha/tirtha-022\"><span class=\"max-w-[10rem] truncate sm:max-w-xs\">Shri Hrinkar Parshwanath</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></a></nav></div></main><footer class=\"mt-auto border-t border-sandstone-deep/60 py-8\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 font-ui text-xs text-ink-soft flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-2 sm:items-center sm:justify-between\"><p>१०८ पार्श्वनाथ तीर्थ दर्शन — श्री पार्श्वनाथ भगवान के तीर्थों का डिजिटल संकलन</p><p>Original source: Rajendra Kumar Jain, Parshv Sadan, Parshv Nagar, Dungarpur</p></div></footer><!--$--><!--/$--><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/40e0f9pufs6g4.js\" id=\"_R_\" async=\"\"></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1:\\\"$Sreact.fragment\\\"\\n2:I[20256,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/3vsl20q6wdw12.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0abm728svpw4d.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\\\"],\\\"SessionBootstrap\\\"]\\n3:I[39756,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/3vsl20q6wdw12.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0abm728svpw4d.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n4:I[37457,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/3vsl20q6wdw12.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0abm728svpw4d.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\\\"],\\\"default\\\"]\\n5:I[22016,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/3vsl20q6wdw12.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0abm728svpw4d.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/14mrh2-p_w84d.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/2nzzixgj4wils.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/0taliq9wft957.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/3ppkpjc789k8m.js\\\"],\\\"