es of India.. Scripture References: Muleva Parshwanath is mentioned in \\\"365 Shri Parshwadev Jin Nammala,\\\" \\\"Shri Sankeshwar Parshwanath Chhand,\\\" \\\"108 Naam Garbhit Shri Parshwanath Bhavan,\\\" and others. There is an image of Muleva (Moraiya) Parshwanath at the Jiravala crossroads.. Hymn of Praise: Who is the root of all prosperity and success, and the root of all progress, who is the root of the wealth, peace and happiness of Rajnagari (Ahmedabad), whose powerful darshan draws devotees here every day -- \\\"I bow with devotion to Shri Muleva Prabhu Parshwa.\\\". Chanting Mantra: Om Hrim Arh Shri Muleva Parshwanathaya Namah.. Trust: Shri Muleva Parshwanath Shwetambar Jain Tirth, Relief Road, near Panjrapole, Ahmedabad - 380001, State of Gujarat, India. Phone: 079-22123704.. Some further verses are also recorded following the Shri 108 Parshwanath Stuti, which mention the names of Lords Parshwanath such as Sukhsagara, Muhari, Posina, Shankheshwara, Vighnapahari, Nagphana, Kalyan Paras, Manoranjan and Sultan, offering salutations to Shankheshwar Parshwanath.. 19. Shri Hrinkar Parshwanath. This temple is located in Kalushi ni Pol, Kalupur, Ahmedabad-380001.. Main Deity: The main deity of this temple is Bhagwan Sambhavnath. In the padmasana posture, a beautiful black-colored image, 25 centimeters tall, set within a beautifully carved parikar, is that of Bhagwan Hrinkar Parshwanath. Behind the image is a canopy of 7 serpent hoods. This image is in the basement, beside the image of Bhagwan Chintamani Parshwanath.. Location: This is in the temple of Bhagwan Sambhavnath in Kalushi ni Pol, Ahmedabad.. History: In mantra literature, \\\"Hrim\\\" is considered a mantra-seed (bija). This mantra-seed contains within it the establishment of the twenty-four Jineshwars. Mantra scripture describes a method of meditating on Lord Parshwanath positioned at the center of the syllable \\\"Hrim,\\\" for the practice of numerous yantras and the contemplation of mantras. As though the Lord had manifested in a radiant form directly from such meditation, this image resides in the basement (bhoyaru) of the shrine of Shri Sambhavnath Bhagwan in Kalushi ni Pol, beside Shri Chintamani Parshwanath Prabhu. This Lord, established in the form of \\\"Hrim,\\\" is renowned by the name Hrinkar Parshwanath. Since ancient times, Jainism has existed in Gujarat with a large population of Jains living here. The holiest Jain temples -- such as Shatrunjay Mahatirth, Girnar Tirth, and Shankheshwar Tirth -- are in Gujarat. Most Jain pilgrimage sites are in Gujarat. The image of the main deity, Shri Sambhavnath Bhagwan, bears an inscription of Vikram Samvat 1527, and the image of the main deity of the upper floor, Shri Shantinath, bears an inscription of Vikram Samvat 1670. This indicates that this temple is more than 500 years old. The old temple was renovated in Vikram Samvat 2020, and the images were reconsecrated on the 10th day of the month of Shravan in Vikram Samvat 2021, by the revered hands of Acharya Shri Jambusurishwarji.. 1. The main temple of Hrinkar Parshwanath is in Kalushi Pol, Ahmedabad. 2. In the city of Dungarpur, there is a metal image of Shri Hrinkar Parshwanath in the home temple of Shri Gordhandasji Patwa, which was installed by the revered hands of Acharya Shri Vijaysurishwarji in the latter half of the 17th century. 3. In Belgaum, Karnataka, there is a chariot-shaped temple of Bhagwan Shri Hrinkar Parshwanath. This temple was built by the Shri Rajasthan Jain Shwetambar Murtipujak Trust, and the image was installed in the month of Paush Vadi in Vikram Samvat 2057...\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"https://goo.gl/maps/SqstUAcbekSf6BhB8\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_blank\\\",\\\"rel\\\":\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-sm 