 ago, a family of Shethjis of the Shrimali Visha caste built a temple in Idalpur (a suburb of Ahmedabad) and formally installed the image of Muleva Parshwanath there. It is believed that over time the temple must have fallen into disrepair, and this image of Muleva Parshwanath was brought to Panjrapole and installed in the temple of Bhagwan Adinath. Today's Haripura was earlier known as Idalpur. The image of Muleva Parshwanath is very powerful, striking and beautiful. Devotees who worship this image regularly experience its influence. Many devotees in Ahmedabad begin their daily routine after worshipping at this temple of Muleva Parshwanath. It is believed that no devotee can continuously worship this image of Muleva Parshwanath for 6 months. This temple is managed by the Seth Hathisingh Kesarisingh Trust. The temple was recently rebuilt without moving the images. This impressive temple is well worth a visit. This temple is also known as the \\\"Moraiya Parshwanath Temple.\\\"\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"article\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"prose-none space-y-4 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.85] text-ink\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"18. Shri Muleva Parshwanath\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Main Deity: An image of Bhagwan Muleva Parshwanath in the padmasana posture, white in color, approximately 28.5 inches tall and 22 inches wide, stands beside the image of the main deity, Shri Adinath Bhagwan. This is in Ahmedabad.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Location: This is on Relief Road in Ahmedabad city.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"$23\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Other Temples: Ahmedabad has more than 400 temples.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"5\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Directions: Ahmedabad is a very famous city of Gujarat. It is well connected by rail, road and air 